    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107697" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρμετρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beyond all measure,
				excessive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτῆσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					864d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολάσεις, ὀργαί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				pp.52,61
			</span></i> W.; of a tumour, <i><span class="en">
				Leonid.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				15.5
			</span></i>. Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽ ὑπερμέτρως ἄλγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					418
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>going beyond the metre,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				6.2
			</span></i>.</div>
